      "writtenOn": "2025-10-27T16:13:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The \"until an alternative arrives\" is the key phrase. If we just pollute android-mainline with hooks, then no one ever checks if there is an alternative or attempts to create one.\n\nOur general policy is to accept hooks and other out-of-tree patches into android-mainline to support testing of android-mainline. Most of the hooks you see in android mainline are needed for pre/post-submit testing with Pixel.\n\nIf we know for sure that no \"alternative will arrive\" and it is needed in the future, we could consider it. If it becomes needed for pre/post-submit testing of android-mainline, we\u0027d definitely accept it.",
      "parentUuid": "630effab_92e4cb27",
      "revId": "68c8ff49f121272a2fc825dc7514ccac9c05c73e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
